/-!
# A separable point of small degree on an affine plane curve

Let `k` be an infinite field and `f ∈ k[x, y]`. A point of the affine plane curve `V(f)` at
which `V(f) → Spec(k)` is smooth is, by the Jacobian criterion of [Stacks, Tag 00TE] in two
variables and one equation, a prime `p ⊇ (f)` avoiding one of the two derivatives `pderiv i f` of
`f`. This file produces from such a prime a *closed* point with the same property whose residue
field is a finite separable extension of `k` of degree at most `deg(f)`.

The construction is the explicit one of [Stacks, Tag 0CCU]. Write `f = g · h` with `g` an
irreducible factor of `f` lying in `p`; because `∂f/∂y ∉ p` the factor `g` occurs in `f` with
multiplicity one and `∂g/∂y ≠ 0`. Over the field of fractions `k(x)` the polynomial `g` is
irreducible of positive degree in `y`, so it is coprime to `∂g/∂y` and to `h`; clearing
denominators in the two Bézout identities produces `c, c' ∈ k[x]` with `c, c' ∈ (g, ∂g/∂y)`
respectively `(g, h)`. Since `k` is infinite there is `t ∈ k` at which neither `c`, nor `c'`,
nor the leading coefficient of `g` in `y` vanishes. Then `g(t, y)` has the same `y`-degree as
`g`, is separable, and is coprime to `h(t, y)`; any monic irreducible factor `q` of `g(t, y)`
is separable and divides neither `∂g/∂y(t, y)` nor `h(t, y)`, so the kernel of
`k[x, y] → k[y]/(q)`, `x ↦ t`, contains `f` but not `∂f/∂y`, and its residue field
`k[y]/(q)` is separable over `k` of degree `deg_y q ≤ deg_y g ≤ deg f`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Curves.exists_isMaximal_notMem_derivative`: the statement for `k[x₁, …, xₘ][y]`, where
  the derivative is the one in the last variable. This is where the mathematics happens.
* `Stacks.Curves.exists_isMaximal_notMem_pderiv`,
  `Stacks.Curves.exists_isMaximal_notMem_pderiv_of_index`: the same for
  `MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) k`, differentiating in the variable `0` and in an arbitrary
  variable.
* `Stacks.Curves.exists_isMaximal_isSeparable_finrank_le_totalDegree`: **Tag 0CCU** for the
  affine plane curve, with the degree bound in terms of the total degree of `f` and with
  smoothness in the Jacobian form of [Stacks, Tag 00TE].

## Implementation notes

The proof is run in `Polynomial (MvPolynomial (Fin n) k)`, where the distinguished variable is
the outer one and `Polynomial.derivative` is the derivative with respect to it, and transported
to `MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) k` along `MvPolynomial.finSuccEquiv`;
`Stacks.Curves.finSuccEquiv_pderiv_zero` is the compatibility of that equivalence with the
derivative `pderiv` in the split-off variable, which Mathlib does not record. Changing the
distinguished variable is a transport along `MvPolynomial.renameEquiv (Equiv.swap i 0)`, so both
indices of the plane are covered by one argument.

Smoothness is not mentioned. The hypothesis is the Jacobian condition `∂f/∂xᵢ ∉ p` that
[Stacks, Tag 00TE] — available here as
`Algebra.Presentation.isSmoothAt_iff_exists_jacobian_notMem` — identifies with smoothness at the
corresponding point for a presentation by one equation in two variables, and the conclusion
carries the same condition at the closed point that is produced. A maximal ideal of `k[x, y]`
containing `f` is a closed point of `V(f)` and `k[x, y] ⧸ m` is its residue field, so no
scheme-theoretic language is needed to state either.

Bézout identities are cleared of denominators with `IsLocalization.integerNormalization` rather
than with a resultant: `Polynomial.isUnit_resultant_iff_isCoprime` needs a monic polynomial, and
`g` is not monic in `y` over `k[x]`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CCU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CCU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00TE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00TE)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open Polynomial MvPolynomial

universe u

namespace Stacks.Curves

/-! ### Separability of a simple extension -/

/-- An extension generated by one separable element is separable. -/
private theorem isSeparable_of_adjoin_eq_top {k L : Type*} [Field k] [Field L] [Algebra k L]
    (x : L) (hx : IsSeparable k x) (htop : Algebra.adjoin k ({x} : Set L) = ⊤) :
    Algebra.IsSeparable k L := by
  have h1 : Algebra.IsSeparable k (IntermediateField.adjoin k ({x} : Set L)) :=
    (IntermediateField.isSeparable_adjoin_simple_iff_isSeparable k L).2 hx
  have h2 : IntermediateField.adjoin k ({x} : Set L) = ⊤ := by
    apply IntermediateField.toSubalgebra_injective
    rw [IntermediateField.adjoin_simple_toSubalgebra_of_isAlgebraic hx.isIntegral.isAlgebraic,
      htop]
    rfl
  rw [h2] at h1
  exact (IntermediateField.isSeparable_top k L).1 h1

/-- The field obtained by adjoining a root of a monic irreducible separable polynomial is a
separable extension. -/
private theorem isSeparable_adjoinRoot {k : Type u} [Field k] {q : Polynomial k}
    (hq : Irreducible q) (hm : q.Monic) (hs : q.Separable) :
    haveI : Fact (Irreducible q) := ⟨hq⟩
    Algebra.IsSeparable k (AdjoinRoot q) := by
  have : Fact (Irreducible q) := ⟨hq⟩
  refine isSeparable_of_adjoin_eq_top (AdjoinRoot.root q) ?_ AdjoinRoot.adjoinRoot_eq_top
  have h : minpoly k (AdjoinRoot.root q) = q := by
    rw [AdjoinRoot.minpoly_root hq.ne_zero, hm.leadingCoeff]; simp
  rw [IsSeparable, h]; exact hs

/-- The quotient map onto `AdjoinRoot q`, as a homomorphism of `k`-algebras. -/
private def adjoinRootMkAlgHom {k : Type u} [Field k] (q : Polynomial k) :
    Polynomial k →ₐ[k] AdjoinRoot q :=
  { AdjoinRoot.mk q with commutes' := fun _ => rfl }

/-! ### Quotients by the kernel of a surjection onto a field -/

/-- The kernel of a surjection of `k`-algebras onto a field is a maximal ideal whose quotient is,
as a `k`-algebra, that field. -/
private theorem exists_isMaximal_ker {k : Type u} {A : Type u} {L : Type u} [Field k]
    [CommRing A] [Algebra k A] [Field L] [Algebra k L] (φ : A →ₐ[k] L)
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective φ) [Module.Finite k L] [Algebra.IsSeparable k L] :
    ∃ M : Ideal A, M.IsMaximal ∧ (∀ x : A, x ∈ M ↔ φ x = 0) ∧
      Module.Finite k (A ⧸ M) ∧ Algebra.IsSeparable k (A ⧸ M) ∧
      Module.finrank k (A ⧸ M) = Module.finrank k L := by
  have e : (A ⧸ RingHom.ker φ) ≃ₐ[k] L := Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective hsurj
  exact ⟨RingHom.ker φ, Ideal.Quotient.maximal_of_isField _
      (MulEquiv.isField (Field.toIsField L) e.toRingEquiv.toMulEquiv),
    fun _ => RingHom.mem_ker, Module.Finite.equiv e.symm.toLinearEquiv,
    AlgEquiv.Algebra.isSeparable e.symm, e.toLinearEquiv.finrank_eq⟩

/-- Transport of the conclusion along an isomorphism of `k`-algebras: a prime of `A` is carried to
the prime of `B` to which the conclusion is applied, and a maximal ideal of `B` is pulled back. -/
private theorem exists_isMaximal_comap {k : Type u} {A B : Type u} [Field k] [CommRing A]
    [CommRing B] [Algebra k A] [Algebra k B] (E : A ≃ₐ[k] B) {x y : A} {d : ℕ}
    {p : Ideal A} (hp : p.IsPrime) (hx : x ∈ p) (hy : y ∉ p)
    (H : ∀ q : Ideal B, q.IsPrime → E x ∈ q → E y ∉ q → ∃ M' : Ideal B, M'.IsMaximal ∧
      E x ∈ M' ∧ E y ∉ M' ∧ Module.Finite k (B ⧸ M') ∧ Algebra.IsSeparable k (B ⧸ M') ∧
      Module.finrank k (B ⧸ M') ≤ d) :
    ∃ M : Ideal A, M.IsMaximal ∧ x ∈ M ∧ y ∉ M ∧ Module.Finite k (A ⧸ M) ∧
      Algebra.IsSeparable k (A ⧸ M) ∧ Module.finrank k (A ⧸ M) ≤ d := by
  obtain ⟨M', hM', hx', hy', hfin, hsep, hrank⟩ := H (Ideal.comap E.symm.toAlgHom p)
    (Ideal.comap_isPrime _ _) (by simpa using hx) (by simpa using hy)
  have _ := hfin
  have _ := hsep
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective E.toAlgHom := E.surjective
  have hq : (A ⧸ Ideal.comap E.toAlgHom M') ≃ₐ[k] B ⧸ M' :=
    Ideal.quotientEquivAlg _ M' E (Ideal.map_comap_of_surjective _ hsurj M').symm
  exact ⟨Ideal.comap E.toAlgHom M', Ideal.comap_isMaximal_of_surjective _ hsurj, hx', hy',
    Module.Finite.equiv hq.symm.toLinearEquiv, AlgEquiv.Algebra.isSeparable hq.symm,
    (le_of_eq hq.toLinearEquiv.finrank_eq).trans hrank⟩

/-! ### Specializing a Bézout identity -/

/-- A nonzero polynomial over an infinite field is nonzero at some point. -/
private theorem exists_aeval_ne_zero {k : Type u} [Field k] [Infinite k] {ι : Type*}
    (p : MvPolynomial ι k) (hp : p ≠ 0) : ∃ x : ι → k, MvPolynomial.aeval x p ≠ 0 := by
  by_contra hc
  push Not at hc
  refine hp (MvPolynomial.funext fun x => ?_)
  rw [map_zero, ← MvPolynomial.aeval_eq_eval]
  exact hc x

/-- A Bézout identity with a constant right-hand side specializes to coprimality wherever that
constant does not vanish. -/
private theorem isCoprime_map_of_mul_add_mul_eq_C {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {k : Type*} [Field k]
    (ev : R →+* k) {g d a b : Polynomial R} {c : R} (hc : ev c ≠ 0)
    (he : a * g + b * d = Polynomial.C c) :
    IsCoprime (g.map ev) (d.map ev) := by
  refine ⟨Polynomial.C (ev c)⁻¹ * a.map ev, Polynomial.C (ev c)⁻¹ * b.map ev, ?_⟩
  have h2 := congrArg (Polynomial.map ev) he
  rw [Polynomial.map_add, Polynomial.map_mul, Polynomial.map_mul, Polynomial.map_C] at h2
  have hu : Polynomial.C (ev c)⁻¹ * Polynomial.C (ev c) = 1 := by
    rw [← Polynomial.C_mul, inv_mul_cancel₀ hc, Polynomial.C_1]
  linear_combination Polynomial.C (ev c)⁻¹ * h2 + hu

/-- Two polynomials coprime over the field of fractions generate an ideal meeting the
coefficient ring in a nonzero element: clearing denominators in a Bézout identity. -/
private theorem exists_mul_add_mul_eq_C_of_isCoprime_map {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R]
    (K : Type*) [Field K] [Algebra R K] [IsFractionRing R K] {g d : Polynomial R}
    (h : IsCoprime (g.map (algebraMap R K)) (d.map (algebraMap R K))) :
    ∃ (c : R) (a b : Polynomial R), c ≠ 0 ∧ a * g + b * d = Polynomial.C c := by
  obtain ⟨α, β, hαβ⟩ := h
  obtain ⟨c₁, hc₁, e₁⟩ := IsLocalization.integerNormalization_spec (nonZeroDivisors R) α
  obtain ⟨c₂, hc₂, e₂⟩ := IsLocalization.integerNormalization_spec (nonZeroDivisors R) β
  refine ⟨c₁ * c₂, Polynomial.C c₂ * IsLocalization.integerNormalization (nonZeroDivisors R) α,
    Polynomial.C c₁ * IsLocalization.integerNormalization (nonZeroDivisors R) β,
    mul_ne_zero (nonZeroDivisors.ne_zero hc₁) (nonZeroDivisors.ne_zero hc₂), ?_⟩
  apply Polynomial.map_injective (algebraMap R K) (IsFractionRing.injective R K)
  simp only [Polynomial.map_add, Polynomial.map_mul, Polynomial.map_C, e₁, e₂,
    Algebra.smul_def, Polynomial.algebraMap_apply, map_mul]
  linear_combination (Polynomial.C (algebraMap R K c₁) * Polynomial.C (algebraMap R K c₂)) * hαβ

/-- A polynomial over a field which is coprime to its derivative and to `H` has a monic
irreducible separable factor dividing neither its derivative nor `H`. -/
private theorem exists_monic_irreducible_separable_dvd {k : Type*} [Field k]
    {G H : Polynomial k} (hG0 : G ≠ 0) (hGnu : ¬ IsUnit G)
    (hcd : IsCoprime G (derivative G)) (hch : IsCoprime G H) :
    ∃ q : Polynomial k, q.Monic ∧ Irreducible q ∧ q.Separable ∧ q ∣ G ∧
      ¬ q ∣ derivative G ∧ ¬ q ∣ H := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨r, hri, hrd⟩ := WfDvdMonoid.exists_irreducible_factor hGnu hG0
  have hqi : Irreducible (normalize r) := (associated_normalize r).irreducible hri
  have hqd : normalize r ∣ G := (associated_normalize r).symm.dvd.trans hrd
  have hnd : ¬ normalize r ∣ derivative G :=
    hqi.coprime_iff_not_dvd.1 (hcd.of_isCoprime_of_dvd_left hqd)
  refine ⟨normalize r, Polynomial.monic_normalize hri.ne_zero, hqi, ?_, hqd, hnd,
    hqi.coprime_iff_not_dvd.1 (hch.of_isCoprime_of_dvd_left hqd)⟩
  rw [Polynomial.separable_iff_derivative_ne_zero hqi]
  intro hz
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := hqd
  exact hnd (by rw [hu, derivative_mul, hz, zero_mul, zero_add]; exact Dvd.intro _ rfl)

/-! ### The closed point -/

/-- The closed point, once a specialization of the base making the chosen factor separable has
been found. -/
private theorem exists_isMaximal_notMem_derivative_aux {k : Type u} [Field k] {m : ℕ}
    {f g h : Polynomial (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k)} (hfh : f = g * h)
    (evA : MvPolynomial (Fin m) k →ₐ[k] k) (hevsurj : Function.Surjective evA)
    (hdeg : (g.map evA.toRingHom).natDegree = g.natDegree) (hdegg : g.natDegree ≠ 0)
    (hcd : IsCoprime (g.map evA.toRingHom) ((derivative g).map evA.toRingHom))
    (hch : IsCoprime (g.map evA.toRingHom) (h.map evA.toRingHom)) :
    ∃ M : Ideal (Polynomial (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k)), M.IsMaximal ∧ f ∈ M ∧
      derivative f ∉ M ∧
      Module.Finite k (Polynomial (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k) ⧸ M) ∧
      Algebra.IsSeparable k (Polynomial (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k) ⧸ M) ∧
      Module.finrank k (Polynomial (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k) ⧸ M) ≤ g.natDegree := by
  classical
  have hG0 : g.map evA.toRingHom ≠ 0 := fun hz => hdegg (by rw [← hdeg, hz]; simp)
  have hGnu : ¬ IsUnit (g.map evA.toRingHom) := fun hu =>
    hdegg (by rw [← hdeg]; exact Polynomial.natDegree_eq_zero_of_isUnit hu)
  have hder : derivative (g.map evA.toRingHom) = (derivative g).map evA.toRingHom :=
    Polynomial.derivative_map g evA.toRingHom
  obtain ⟨q, hqm, hqi, hqs, hqd, hqnd, hqnh⟩ :=
    exists_monic_irreducible_separable_dvd hG0 hGnu (hder ▸ hcd) hch
  have hfact : Fact (Irreducible q) := ⟨hqi⟩
  have _ : Module.Finite k (AdjoinRoot q) :=
    Module.Finite.of_basis (AdjoinRoot.powerBasis hqi.ne_zero).basis
  have _ : Algebra.IsSeparable k (AdjoinRoot q) := isSeparable_adjoinRoot hqi hqm hqs
  have hfr : Module.finrank k (AdjoinRoot q) = q.natDegree := by
    rw [(AdjoinRoot.powerBasis hqi.ne_zero).finrank, AdjoinRoot.powerBasis_dim]
  have happ : ∀ x : Polynomial (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k),
      ((adjoinRootMkAlgHom q).comp (Polynomial.mapAlgHom evA)) x =
        AdjoinRoot.mk q (x.map evA.toRingHom) := fun _ => rfl
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective ((adjoinRootMkAlgHom q).comp (Polynomial.mapAlgHom evA)) := by
    intro y
    obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := AdjoinRoot.mk_surjective (g := q) y
    obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := Polynomial.map_surjective evA.toRingHom hevsurj z
    exact ⟨w, by rw [happ, hw]; exact hz⟩
  obtain ⟨M, hM, hMmem, hMfin, hMsep, hMrank⟩ := exists_isMaximal_ker _ hsurj
  refine ⟨M, hM, ?_, ?_, hMfin, hMsep, ?_⟩
  · rw [hMmem, happ, hfh, Polynomial.map_mul, AdjoinRoot.mk_eq_zero]
    exact hqd.mul_right _
  · rw [hMmem, happ, hfh, derivative_mul, Polynomial.map_add, Polynomial.map_mul,
      Polynomial.map_mul, AdjoinRoot.mk_eq_zero]
    intro hdvd
    have h1 : q ∣ g.map evA.toRingHom * (derivative h).map evA.toRingHom := hqd.mul_right _
    have h2 : q ∣ (derivative g).map evA.toRingHom * h.map evA.toRingHom :=
      (dvd_add_right h1).mp (by rwa [add_comm] at hdvd)
    rcases (UniqueFactorizationMonoid.irreducible_iff_prime.1 hqi).2.2 _ _ h2 with h3 | h4
    · exact hqnd (hder ▸ h3)
    · exact hqnh h4
  · rw [hMrank, hfr, ← hdeg]
    exact Polynomial.natDegree_le_of_dvd hqd hG0

/-- **A closed point of `V(f)` at which `∂f/∂y` is invertible, with small separable residue
field.** Let `k` be an infinite field and let `f ∈ k[x₁, …, xₘ][y]`. If some prime of
`k[x₁, …, xₘ][y]` contains `f` but not `∂f/∂y`, then some *maximal* ideal does, and its residue
field is a finite separable extension of `k` of degree at most the degree of `f` in `y`. -/
public theorem exists_isMaximal_notMem_derivative {k : Type u} [Field k] [Infinite k] {m : ℕ}
    {f : Polynomial (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k)}
    {p : Ideal (Polynomial (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k))} (hp : p.IsPrime)
    (hfp : f ∈ p) (hdp : derivative f ∉ p) :
    ∃ M : Ideal (Polynomial (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k)), M.IsMaximal ∧ f ∈ M ∧
      derivative f ∉ M ∧
      Module.Finite k (Polynomial (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k) ⧸ M) ∧
      Algebra.IsSeparable k (Polynomial (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k) ⧸ M) ∧
      Module.finrank k (Polynomial (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k) ⧸ M) ≤ f.natDegree := by
  classical
  have hdf0 : derivative f ≠ 0 := fun hz => hdp (hz ▸ p.zero_mem)
  have hf0 : f ≠ 0 := fun hz => hdf0 (by rw [hz, derivative_zero])
  -- an irreducible factor of `f` lying in `p`
  have hprod : (UniqueFactorizationMonoid.factors f).prod ∈ p := by
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := (UniqueFactorizationMonoid.factors_prod hf0).symm.dvd
    exact hc ▸ Ideal.mul_mem_right c p hfp
  obtain ⟨g, hgmem, hgp⟩ := (hp.multiset_prod_mem_iff_exists_mem _).1 hprod
  have hgi : Irreducible g := UniqueFactorizationMonoid.irreducible_of_factor g hgmem
  obtain ⟨h, hfh⟩ := UniqueFactorizationMonoid.dvd_of_mem_factors hgmem
  have hgndf : ¬ g ∣ derivative f := by
    rintro ⟨c, hc⟩
    exact hdp (hc ▸ Ideal.mul_mem_right c p hgp)
  -- the factor is simple and has nonzero derivative
  have hdg0 : derivative g ≠ 0 := fun hz =>
    hgndf ⟨derivative h, by rw [hfh, derivative_mul, hz, zero_mul, zero_add]⟩
  have hgnh : ¬ g ∣ h := by
    rintro ⟨c, hc⟩
    exact hgndf ⟨derivative g * c + derivative (g * c), by
      rw [hfh, hc, derivative_mul]; ring⟩
  have hdegg : g.natDegree ≠ 0 := by
    intro hz
    obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := Polynomial.natDegree_eq_zero.1 hz
    exact hdg0 (by rw [← ha]; simp)
  have hprim : g.IsPrimitive := by
    intro a ha
    obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := ha
    rcases hgi.isUnit_or_isUnit hs with h1 | h2
    · exact Polynomial.isUnit_C.1 h1
    · exact absurd (le_antisymm (hs ▸ (Polynomial.natDegree_mul_le (p := Polynomial.C a)
        (q := s)).trans (by simp [Polynomial.natDegree_eq_zero_of_isUnit h2])) (Nat.zero_le _))
        hdegg
  -- coprimality over the field of fractions
  have _inst1 : NormalizationMonoid (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k) :=
    UniqueFactorizationMonoid.strongNormalizationMonoid.toNormalizationMonoid
  have _inst2 : NormalizedGCDMonoid (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k) :=
    UniqueFactorizationMonoid.toNormalizedGCDMonoid (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k)
  have hinj : Function.Injective
      (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k) (FractionRing (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k))) :=
    IsFractionRing.injective _ _
  have hGirr : Irreducible
      (g.map (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k) (FractionRing (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k)))) :=
    (hprim.irreducible_iff_irreducible_map_fraction_map
      (K := FractionRing (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k))).1 hgi
  have hGcopD : IsCoprime
      (g.map (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k) (FractionRing (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k))))
      ((derivative g).map
        (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k) (FractionRing (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k)))) := by
    rw [hGirr.coprime_iff_not_dvd]
    intro hd
    have h1 : (derivative g).map
        (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k) (FractionRing (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k))) ≠ 0 := by
      simpa [Polynomial.map_eq_zero_iff hinj] using hdg0
    have h2 := Polynomial.natDegree_le_of_dvd hd h1
    rw [Polynomial.natDegree_map_eq_of_injective hinj,
      Polynomial.natDegree_map_eq_of_injective hinj] at h2
    exact absurd h2 (not_le.2 (Polynomial.natDegree_derivative_lt hdegg))
  have hGcopH : IsCoprime
      (g.map (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k) (FractionRing (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k))))
      (h.map (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k)
        (FractionRing (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k)))) := by
    rw [hGirr.coprime_iff_not_dvd]
    intro hd
    exact hgnh ((hprim.dvd_iff_fraction_map_dvd_fraction_map
      (FractionRing (MvPolynomial (Fin m) k))).2 hd)
  obtain ⟨c₁, a₁, b₁, hc₁, he₁⟩ := exists_mul_add_mul_eq_C_of_isCoprime_map _ hGcopD
  obtain ⟨c₂, a₂, b₂, hc₂, he₂⟩ := exists_mul_add_mul_eq_C_of_isCoprime_map _ hGcopH
  -- a specialization of the base avoiding all three obstructions
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := exists_aeval_ne_zero (g.leadingCoeff * (c₁ * c₂))
    (mul_ne_zero (Polynomial.leadingCoeff_ne_zero.2 hgi.ne_zero) (mul_ne_zero hc₁ hc₂))
  rw [map_mul, map_mul] at ht
  obtain ⟨M, hM, hfM, hdM, hfin, hsep, hrank⟩ :=
    exists_isMaximal_notMem_derivative_aux hfh (MvPolynomial.aeval (R := k) t)
      (fun a => ⟨MvPolynomial.C a, by simp⟩)
      (Polynomial.natDegree_map_of_leadingCoeff_ne_zero
        (MvPolynomial.aeval (R := k) t).toRingHom (left_ne_zero_of_mul ht)) hdegg
      (isCoprime_map_of_mul_add_mul_eq_C _ (left_ne_zero_of_mul (right_ne_zero_of_mul ht)) he₁)
      (isCoprime_map_of_mul_add_mul_eq_C _ (right_ne_zero_of_mul (right_ne_zero_of_mul ht)) he₂)
  exact ⟨M, hM, hfM, hdM, hfin, hsep,
    hrank.trans (Polynomial.natDegree_le_of_dvd ⟨h, hfh⟩ hf0)⟩

/-! ### Transport to polynomials in several variables -/

/-- `MvPolynomial.finSuccEquiv` carries the derivative `pderiv` in the split-off variable to the
derivative of the resulting one-variable polynomial. -/
public theorem finSuccEquiv_pderiv_zero {k : Type u} [CommRing k] (n : ℕ)
    (f : MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) k) :
    finSuccEquiv k n (pderiv 0 f) = derivative (finSuccEquiv k n f) := by
  induction f using MvPolynomial.induction_on with
  | C a =>
    have h : finSuccEquiv k n (MvPolynomial.C a) = Polynomial.C (MvPolynomial.C a) := by
      simpa [MvPolynomial.algebraMap_eq] using (finSuccEquiv k n).commutes a
    simp [h]
  | add p q hp hq => simp [hp, hq]
  | mul_X p i hp =>
    rcases Fin.eq_zero_or_eq_succ i with rfl | ⟨j, rfl⟩
    · simp [hp, finSuccEquiv_X_zero]; ring
    · simp [hp, finSuccEquiv_X_succ, mul_comm]

/-- **A closed point of `V(f)` at which `∂f/∂x₀` is invertible, with small separable residue
field.** The statement of `Stacks.Curves.exists_isMaximal_notMem_derivative` for
`MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) k`, the distinguished variable being the first one. -/
public theorem exists_isMaximal_notMem_pderiv {k : Type u} [Field k] [Infinite k] {n : ℕ}
    {f : MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) k} {p : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) k)}
    (hp : p.IsPrime) (hfp : f ∈ p) (hdp : pderiv 0 f ∉ p) :
    ∃ M : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) k), M.IsMaximal ∧ f ∈ M ∧ pderiv 0 f ∉ M ∧
      Module.Finite k (MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) k ⧸ M) ∧
      Algebra.IsSeparable k (MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) k ⧸ M) ∧
      Module.finrank k (MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) k ⧸ M) ≤ f.degreeOf 0 := by
  classical
  set e := finSuccEquiv k n with he
  have hder : derivative (e f) = e (pderiv 0 f) := (finSuccEquiv_pderiv_zero n f).symm
  refine exists_isMaximal_comap e hp hfp hdp fun q hq hf hd => ?_
  rw [← hder] at hd
  obtain ⟨M', hM', hfM', hdM', hfin', hsep', hrank'⟩ :=
    exists_isMaximal_notMem_derivative hq hf hd
  exact ⟨M', hM', hfM', hder ▸ hdM', hfin', hsep',
    hrank'.trans (le_of_eq (natDegree_finSuccEquiv f))⟩

/-- **A closed point of `V(f)` at which `∂f/∂xᵢ` is invertible, with small separable residue
field.** The statement of `Stacks.Curves.exists_isMaximal_notMem_pderiv` for an arbitrary
distinguished variable, obtained by permuting the variables. -/
public theorem exists_isMaximal_notMem_pderiv_of_index {k : Type u} [Field k] [Infinite k]
    {n : ℕ} (i : Fin (n + 1)) {f : MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) k}
    {p : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) k)}
    (hp : p.IsPrime) (hfp : f ∈ p) (hdp : pderiv i f ∉ p) :
    ∃ M : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) k), M.IsMaximal ∧ f ∈ M ∧ pderiv i f ∉ M ∧
      Module.Finite k (MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) k ⧸ M) ∧
      Algebra.IsSeparable k (MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) k ⧸ M) ∧
      Module.finrank k (MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) k ⧸ M) ≤ f.degreeOf i := by
  classical
  set σ : Fin (n + 1) ≃ Fin (n + 1) := Equiv.swap i 0 with hσ
  set E := MvPolynomial.renameEquiv k σ with hE
  have hσi : σ i = 0 := Equiv.swap_apply_left i 0
  have hEf : ∀ x : MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) k, E x = rename σ x := fun _ => rfl
  have hder : pderiv 0 (E f) = E (pderiv i f) := by
    rw [hEf, hEf, ← hσi, MvPolynomial.pderiv_rename σ.injective i f]
  refine exists_isMaximal_comap E hp hfp hdp fun q hq hf hd => ?_
  rw [← hder] at hd
  obtain ⟨M', hM', hfM', hdM', hfin', hsep', hrank'⟩ := exists_isMaximal_notMem_pderiv hq hf hd
  refine ⟨M', hM', hfM', hder ▸ hdM', hfin', hsep', hrank'.trans (le_of_eq ?_)⟩
  rw [hEf, ← hσi, MvPolynomial.degreeOf_rename_of_injective σ.injective i]

/-- **The affine input to Tag 0CCU, not itself Tag 0CCU.** Let `k` be an infinite field, let
`f ∈ k[x₀, x₁]`, and suppose some prime of `k[x₀, x₁]` contains `f` but not `∂f/∂xᵢ` — by the
Jacobian criterion of [Stacks, Tag 00TE] in two variables and one equation, that `V(f)` is
smooth over `k` at the corresponding point. Then some *maximal* ideal `m` of `k[x₀, x₁]`
contains `f` and not `∂f/∂xᵢ`, so is a closed point of `V(f)` in the smooth locus, and its
residue field `k[x₀, x₁] ⧸ m` is a finite separable extension of `k` of degree at most the
degree of `f`.

This is purely commutative algebra on the affine coordinate ring: it carries no scheme-theoretic
smoothness notion and does not by itself produce the closed point of the *projective* plane
curve of Tag 0CCU, so the `@[stacks 0CCU]` attribute does not belong here; it belongs on the
covering statement in terms of `Proj` once that statement exists. -/
public theorem exists_isMaximal_isSeparable_finrank_le_totalDegree {k : Type u} [Field k]
    [Infinite k] (i : Fin 2) {f : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k} {p : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k)}
    (hp : p.IsPrime) (hfp : f ∈ p) (hdp : pderiv i f ∉ p) :
    ∃ m : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k), m.IsMaximal ∧ f ∈ m ∧ pderiv i f ∉ m ∧
      Module.Finite k (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k ⧸ m) ∧
      Algebra.IsSeparable k (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k ⧸ m) ∧
      Module.finrank k (MvPolynomial (Fin 2) k ⧸ m) ≤ f.totalDegree := by
  obtain ⟨m, hm, hfm, hdm, hfin, hsep, hrank⟩ :=
    exists_isMaximal_notMem_pderiv_of_index i hp hfp hdp
  exact ⟨m, hm, hfm, hdm, hfin, hsep, hrank.trans (MvPolynomial.degreeOf_le_totalDegree f i)⟩

end Stacks.Curves

